{"title":"Career Roadmap · NGO Conservation Officer","role":"NGO Conservation Officer","summary":"An NGO Conservation Officer works on biodiversity conservation, habitat protection, wildlife monitoring, community-based conservation, environmental education, field research and conservation programmes. The role can involve significant fieldwork, ecological surveys, GIS, data collection, stakeholder coordination, reporting and project management.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starting point"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Wildlife Biology / Ecology / Conservation"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"NGO Conservation Officer"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Wildlife · Biodiversity · Ecology · Conservation"}],[{"text":"Primary work"},{"text":"Field conservation + research + community programmes"}],[{"text":"Core capability"},{"text":"Ecology + field skills + conservation management"}],[{"text":"Important digital skill"},{"text":"GIS + ecological data analysis"}],[{"text":"Important professional skill"},{"text":"Community/stakeholder engagement"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build ecology, biodiversity, field survey and GIS skills"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in species conservation, habitat restoration, human-wildlife conflict or community conservation"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress to Conservation Officer, Programme Coordinator, Conservation Scientist or Project Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Lead large-scale biodiversity programmes, landscape conservation and climate-adaptation initiatives"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc graduate, a practical route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Wildlife Biology